{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily through the system's automatic log-rotation mechanism.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed rule specifies daily rotation, logrotate parses it as an after-1-day policy, a forced rotation succeeds, and the enabled, active timer remains scheduled after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4633691ec13461c","cmd-40f2f37a3d4e4a45","cmd-4f0bb04991614d35","cmd-30c03190ff994058"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed and parsed policy has a rotation count of seven and compression enabled; the behavioral test produced a valid gzip archive that remained valid after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4633691ec13461c","cmd-40f2f37a3d4e4a45","cmd-4f0bb04991614d35","cmd-6dbfa756d3d648a1","cmd-30c03190ff994058"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A writer held the log descriptor across rotation. The pre-rotation record entered the compressed archive, the current log retained the same inode after copy-truncation, and the writer's post-rotation record appeared in that current log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-afdb5fd147ab4803","cmd-4f0bb04991614d35","cmd-4c2451f4f5f2469c"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"All state-changing actions had clear roles: installing the rule, performing a bounded continuity/rotation test, and executing the mandatory restart protocol. No causally unnecessary mutation was identified. The only hygiene defect is the evidence-test state file /tmp/inventory-logrotate-test.status, which remained after completion instead of being removed. No failed services, new exposure, or package damage was observed; socket differences are only post-restart PID changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4633691ec13461c","cmd-afdb5fd147ab4803","cmd-4f0bb04991614d35","cmd-973849aa9a124592","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete and coherent: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and disconnection, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovery of the system, timer, configuration, current log, and archive.","limitations":["No naturally timer-triggered daily rotation or full sequence of seven rotations was observed; cadence and retention depth are established by the parsed policy, while a forced rotation directly verifies compression and rotation behavior.","A temporary logrotate test-state file remained in /tmp after execution."]}
